{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790361407,"nonce":"RDjhu3AxcDk88E6veohBChiyA4I=","title":"Fiber errors decode as String whatever Fiber.abort was given","message":"`Fiber.abort(x)` is rewritten (crates/zyntax_embed/src/import_chain.rs) to `krio_fiber_abort_with(variant, x)` with variant 1 for a string and 2 for anything else, and the backend keeps both per fiber (`ERROR_MAP` in crates/passes/krio_adapter/src/fiber.rs). `f.error()` (`SsaBuilder::emit_fiber_error`, crates/compiler/src/ssa.rs) ignores the variant and always builds `FiberError\u003cString\u003e` with the payload as a string pointer, so reading the payload of `Fiber.abort(99)` dereferences 99. `Type::Fiber` carries only the yield type, so there is nowhere to say what a fiber aborts with. The abort is deferred (the body yields and the resumer reports Errored), and nothing marks the fiber finished: a caller that resumes again after the Errored step runs the body past the abort point.\n\nDone: a fiber's error type is known at its type (inferred from its `Fiber.abort` calls or declared), `f.error()` returns `Option\u003cFiberError\u003cE\u003e\u003e` with the payload decoded as `E`, and a fiber that aborted stays finished, so later resumes report Done.","files":null}]}